stops <- read.csv("CT_traffic_stops/CT_stops.csv")

dim(stops)
colnames(stops)
```


## Identifying Searched Stops
We created a separate dataset of searched stops because our model will predict contraband discovery following a search. We retained the full dataset for comparisons between searched and unsearched stops.
```{r, include=FALSE}
library(dplyr)

searched_stops <- stops %>% filter(search_conducted == TRUE)
dim(searched_stops)
pct <- nrow(searched_stops) / 268669

cat("Searches were conducted in", round(pct * 100, 1), "% of stops.")
```
Searches occurred in 4,487 stops, approximately 1.7% of all stops.


## Summarizing Contraband Discovery
We calculated how frequently contraband was found among searches and among all traffic stops.
```{r, include=FALSE}
stops_with_cb <- searched_stops %>% filter(contraband_found == TRUE)
dim(stops_with_cb)
pct <- nrow(stops_with_cb) / nrow(searched_stops)
pct2 <- nrow(stops_with_cb) / 268669

cat("Contraband was found in", round(pct * 100, 1), "% of searches and", round(100* pct2, 1), "% of all stops.")
```
Contraband was found in 1,530 stops, representing 34.1% of searches and 0.6% of all stops.


## Assessing Missing Data
We counted missing values among searched stops to guide decisions about cleaning the data and selecting predictors.
```{r, echo=FALSE}
missing_counts <- colSums(is.na(searched_stops))
missing_counts[missing_counts >0]
```
Search type had 407 missing values, while driver age and stop time each had six. Arrest status and stop outcome each had 43 missing values.


## Examining Missing Information and Contraband
We calculated the percentage of all searches with both missing information and contraband found. These percentages describe how often the two occurred together, rather than discovery rates among records with missing information.
```{r, include = FALSE}
stops_with_missing_stop_time <- searched_stops %>%
  filter(is.na(stop_time), contraband_found == TRUE)
pct <- nrow(stops_with_missing_stop_time) / nrow(searched_stops)
cat("Contraband was found in", round(pct * 100, 1), "% of searches with n/a stop_time.\n")

stops_with_missing_search_type <- searched_stops %>%
  filter(is.na(search_type), contraband_found == TRUE)
pct <- nrow(stops_with_missing_search_type) / nrow(searched_stops)
cat("Contraband was found in", round(pct * 100, 1), "% of searches with n/a search_type.\n")

stops_with_missing_is_arrested <- searched_stops %>%
  filter(is.na(is_arrested), contraband_found == TRUE)
pct <- nrow(stops_with_missing_is_arrested) / nrow(searched_stops)
cat("Contraband was found in", round(pct * 100, 1), "% of searches with n/a is_arrested.\n")

stops_with_missing_stop_outcome <- searched_stops %>%
  filter(is.na(stop_outcome), contraband_found == TRUE)
pct <- nrow(stops_with_missing_stop_outcome) / nrow(searched_stops)
cat("Contraband was found in", round(pct * 100, 1), "% of searches with n/a stop_outcome.")
```
To assess whether records with missing information included positive contraband findings, we examined their overlap. Of all searched stops, 1.6% had both missing search type and contraband found; 0.1% had missing arrest status and contraband found, and 0.1% had missing stop outcome and contraband found. The corresponding percentage for missing stop time rounded to 0.0%. These percentages use all searched stops as the denominator.

