## Cleaning and Preparing Predictors
We created a separate cleaned dataset to preserve the original data. We retained standardized variables and county name, removing raw duplicates, constant columns, and detailed location fields to simplify the analysis. We excluded stop outcome and arrest status as potential predictors because they may reflect consequences of contraband discovery. Missing search types were labeled "Unknown" to retain those observations.
```{r, include=FALSE}
cleaned_searches <- searched_stops %>%
  select(-county_fips,
         -location_raw,
         -driver_age_raw,
         -driver_race_raw,
         -search_type_raw,
         -violation_raw,
         -state,
         -police_department,
         -fine_grained_location,
         -stop_outcome,
         -is_arrested) %>%
  mutate(
    county_name = factor(county_name),
    search_type = factor(
      ifelse(is.na(search_type), "Unknown", as.character(search_type))
    )
  )
```
The cleaned dataset retains all 4,487 searched stops. Missing ages and stop times remain unchanged while we evaluate how to handle them.


## Exploring the Age Distribution
We examined driver age among searched stops to assess skewness and the potential need for a transformation.
```{r, echo=FALSE}
plot(density(cleaned_searches$driver_age, na.rm=TRUE),
     main = "Distribution of driver_age",
     xlab = "Driver age (years)",
     col = "purple",
     lwd = 2)
```
The age distribution among drivers whose vehicles were searched is right-skewed, with most ages concentrated in the 20s and fewer drivers at older ages. The long right tail suggests that an age transformation may help reduce skewness. We will compare the original distribution with transformed values before deciding whether to transform age.


## Comparing Age by Contraband Outcome
We compared driver ages between searches that found contraband and those that did not to explore age's relationship with the outcome.
```{r, echo=FALSE}
boxplot(driver_age ~ contraband_found,
        data = cleaned_searches,
        names = c("Not found", "Found"),
        main = "Driver Age by Contraband Search Outcome",
        xlab = "Contraband outcome",
        ylab = "Driver age (years)",
        col = c("lightblue", "lightgreen"))
```
Among searched drivers, those for whom contraband was found had a slightly lower median age, approximately 25 years, compared with approximately 28 years for those for whom contraband was not found. The contraband-found group also had a smaller interquartile range, indicating less variability in the middle 50% of ages. Both groups had older-age outliers and substantial overlap. These results suggest an association between age and contraband discovery, but age alone does not clearly distinguish the two outcomes.
